ient.get` in `weather.py` now retries when the server returns 503. It makes at most 3 attempts in total, waiting 0.5s and then 1s between them. I tested it against a real local HTTP server and all four cases behaved as expected:\n\n| Server responses | Result | Requests made | Waits |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 503, 503, 200 | JSON returned | 3 | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 503, 503, 503 | 503 error raised | 3 (stops there) | 0.5s, 1.0s |\n| 500 | 500 error raised | 1 | none |\n| 200 | JSON returned | 1 | none |\n\n- **Only 503 is retried.** Other HTTP errors and network errors (timeouts, refused connections) are raised straight away, as before.\n- **After the third 503**, the original error is raised so callers still see the real cause.\n- **Settings:** `max_attempts = 3` and `backoff_base = 0.5` are class attributes. The constructor takes a new optional `sleep` argument (default `time.sleep`) so tests can skip the real waits. Existing calls don't need to change.\n- Each failed 503 response is closed before the next try, so no connections are left open.\n\nThe repo has no test suite, so I didn't add test files; the smoke test above is the only check.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 1, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 0, "requests_cache_write": 178202, "requests_cost_usd": 0.924358, "requests_count": 5, "requests_input_uncached": 12, "requests_output": 1665, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-netclient:claude-opus-5-5:trial24", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 107, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T03:51:49.166405+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 20.919, "t_checker_s": 5.444, "t_env_setup_s": 0.0, "task": "trig-omp-netclient", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "off", "thinking_sent": ["none", "none", "none", "none", "non